# Rottenmouth Viper's punishment, one choice for each blight counter: a permanent already chosen to sacrifice is not chosen
# again, and each sacrifice or discard chosen is exactly one, never none (the rulings, CR 101.4). On turn 1 the Viper enters
# with one counter and Bot2 discards a card; it may not discard nothing. On turn 2 Bot2 casts Memnite and Ornithopter. On turn
# 3 the Viper attacks with its second counter and Bot2 chooses to sacrifice twice: it may not sacrifice nothing, and after
# choosing Memnite the second sacrifice is Ornithopter. Both go at once, and the Viper's 6 combat damage takes Bot2 to 14.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Show and Tell
Rottenmouth Viper
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Ornithopter
Lightning Bolt x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Show and Tell.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Rottenmouth Viper)
Bot2.Choose()
Bot2.Modes(Discard a card)
! Bot2.Choose()
Bot2.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Rottenmouth Viper > Bot2)
Bot2.Modes(Sacrifice a nonland permanent)
! Bot2.Choose()
Bot2.Choose(Memnite)
Bot2.Modes(Sacrifice a nonland permanent)
Bot2.Choose(Ornithopter)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter; Memnite; Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
Bot2.Life = 14
